  "structural_fact_ecc2k130": "ord_131(2)=130 so x^131-1 = (x+1)*(irreducible deg 130); 131 is prime so there is no proper subfield. The only Frobenius-stable F_2-SUBSPACE dimensions are 0,1,130,131, so the subfield and frobenius structures here do not exist at 131. Frobenius-invariant factor BASES (sets) do exist: the weight-2 ONB base (14 orbits) and Couveignes-Lercier sets (Galbraith-Granger-Merz-Petit, SAC 2020, ePrint 2020/1315). Their saving is ~n fewer relations and ~n^2 smaller linear algebra, not a lower D*.",
  "reproduce": [
    "sage factor_base_dor.sage --field 8 --dim 4 --selftest 8",
    "sage factor_base_dor.sage --field 7 --dim 3 --targets 127 --seed S --structures frobenius,random,standard   # S=1..6",
    "sage factor_base_dor.sage --field 11 --dim 5 --targets 48 --seed S --structures standard,random   # S=1..3",
    "sage factor_base_dor.sage --field 11 --dim 5 --targets 160 --seed S --structures nb_window,nb_break   # S=1..5",
    "sage factor_base_dor.sage --field 9 --dim 4 --targets 200 --seed S --structures nb_window,nb_break   # S=1..5"
  ],
